FUN_1000_5051: DGROUP near-pointer segment-base restore + far-call vector re-base.

First blocker AFTER the timer spin cleared (patches 016-019). FUN_1000_515e calls FUN_1000_5051 with
param_3 = 0x4fa, a NEAR pointer into DGROUP (DS=0x1c00, which the function itself saves to DAT_1000_595b).
The engine reads/writes the pointed-to structure via `ds:[bx+2]` (byte flags &0xbf|0x22|0x60) and
`ds:[bx]` (word); Ghidra typed param_3 as a raw `undefined2 *` and dereferenced the bare offset as a
host address -> SIGSEGV. Class: DGROUP near-pointer base loss threaded as a pointer param (docs/stage1.md).
Fix: base every param_3 / DAT_1000_5957 deref at g_mem + 0x1c000 + offset. Additionally the final
`call dword cs:0x5951` (far ptr assembled at linear 0x15951 from DAT_1000_5951/5953) was mis-based by
Ghidra to DAT_2000_1951 (0x21951); read the dword at 0x15951 instead. Asm-verified base-0 0x15051..0x150c7.
